                        "goal": "Goal 14. Life below water",
                      
                        "priority": "Enhancement of Polish seaports position, increase in competitiveness of sea transport and ensurance of sea security",
                      
                        "definition": "Number of passengers who arrived at or departed from Polish seaports on passenger ships, cargo vessels and ferries in international traffic.",
                      
                        "unit": "persons",
                      
                        "dimensions": "passenger traffic: arrivals, departures",
                      
                        "methodology": "International traffic covers passengers who arrived during the reference year from foreign ports to Polish ports as their destination ports in their sea journey, as well as the number of passengers who departed on a sea voyage from Polish ports to foreign ports on passenger ships, cargo vessels and ferries.A seaport is an economic facility located at the interface between land and sea, appropriately equipped in technical, technological and organisational terms to handle trade flows carried out by sea, as well as to service maritime and land transport modes involved in their carriage.",
                      
